{"name":"Brown Derby","hex":"#594537","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"derby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several annual horse races.","Any organized race."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/derby"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brown Derby","blocks":[{"text":"Brown Derby was a chain of restaurants in Los Angeles, California. The first and best known was shaped like a derby hat, an iconic image that became synonymous with the Golden Age of Hollywood. It was opened by Wilson Mizner in 1926. The chain was started by Robert H. Cobb and Herbert K. Somborn in the 1920s. The original Brown Derby restaurants had closed or had been converted to other uses by the 1980s, though a Disney-backed Brown Derby national franchising program revived the brand in the 21st century. It is often incorrectly thought that the Brown Derby was a single restaurant, and the Wilshire Boulevard and Hollywood branches are frequently confused."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Brown_Derby_Restaurant%2C_Los_Angeles%2C_Kodachrome_by_Chalmers_Butterfield.jpg/330px-Brown_Derby_Restaurant%2C_Los_Angeles%2C_Kodachrome_by_Chalmers_Butterfield.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_Derby"},{"title":"Brown Derby (actor)","blocks":[{"text":"Brown Derby was a Scottish stage, film and television actor. He made his film debut as Edith Evans's footman in Thorold Dickinson's classic The Queen of Spades (1949). He played Sergeant Roberts, too, in Suspended Alibi. Derby had a regular role as Scott-Erskine in the BBC's The Omega Factor, and also starred in Dr. Finlay's Casebook, Z-Cars, The Saint, Sutherland's Law, Play for Today, Take The High Road and many other British television shows."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/df/Actor_Brown_Derby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_Derby_(actor)"},{"title":"Derby","blocks":[{"text":"Derby is a cathedral city and unitary authority area on the River Derwent in Derbyshire, England. Derbyshire is named after Derby, which was its original county town. As a unitary authority, Derby is administratively independent from Derbyshire County Council. The population of Derby is 275,344 (2025)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Derby_Cathedral_at_night.jpg/330px-Derby_Cathedral_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Derby"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Brown_Derby_on_Wilshire_entrance_1956.JPG/500px-Brown_Derby_on_Wilshire_entrance_1956.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Brown_Derby_on_Wilshire_entrance_1956.JPG/500px-Brown_Derby_on_Wilshire_entrance_1956.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Entrance to the restaurant in 1956","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrown_Derby_on_Wilshir